# Acquisition and integrations

Use `docs/implementation/agent_reference_index.md` to locate INTG contracts, Phase 010 Group 04, Implementation 003, and the active adapter plan.

Catastrophic-error guardrails:

- target-environment capability must be verified; vendor documentation alone is not deployment proof;
- raw vendor response objects are adapter evidence, not canonical DMTZ domain models;
- source-native IDs remain provenance/binding inputs, not canonical identities by convenience;
- partial pagination/window/partition coverage ≠ complete acquisition;
- adapter error, timeout, throttle, 401/403, retention expiry, unsupported surface, parser/schema failure, or unknown coverage ≠ negative domain fact;
- do not advance a checkpoint past unproven coverage;
- reconciliation is the correctness path; streams/webhooks/incremental reads are accelerators unless explicitly proven otherwise;
- retries/redelivery must be idempotent at canonical evidence identity;
- acquisition/integration health is distinct from monitored-domain health;
- quota exhaustion degrades freshness/coverage and is represented explicitly.

Record run/attempt/request/page/window/checkpoint/capability revision and normalization provenance needed to explain what was or was not observed.
